Add the umb-block-grid CSS rules to site.css, then build. The grid container needs display:grid styling. Umbraco's default block grid CSS is only in backoffice preview; on the front end we provide our own:

```css
.umb-block-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(var(--umb-block-grid--grid-columns, 12), minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1.5rem; }
.umb-block-grid__layout-container { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(var(--umb-block-grid--grid-columns, 12), minmax(0, 1fr)); grid-auto-rows: minmax(min-content, auto); gap: 1.5rem; }
.umb-block-grid__layout-item { grid-column: span var(--umb-block-grid--item-column-span, 12) / span var(--umb-block-grid--item-column-span, 12); }
```

Then npm build in Frontend. Then stop Umbraco, dotnet build, restart.

